-- title:
--   Shared source-bank construction is charged to the encoder count
-- statement:
--   For $n>0$ and independent source lengths $N_L,N_R\le n$, instantiate the source-bank constructor at the actual band size, local half-size, block count, and total size. Its time is at most $$\bigl(F(h,J)(232\mu+2)+1300\bigr)\operatorname{encoderCount}(n)+1220,$$ where $F$ is the catalog-program factor and $\mu$ is the total block size.
--
--   This estimate charges original-band source reuse to encoder construction without adding a new per-query input scan.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/Anchen0823/three-sum-1960614/blob/8c25c0325de5be4286413f39ca0c9278aad33f52/Submission/ThreeSum/SourceBandBanksCosts.lean#L54-L75

